  ### Summary                                                                 
                                                                              
  This PR addresses FLYBYME/surfdns#39 by serving the site's                  
  ExposureDescriptor over HTTP and promoting contract gates to runtime data in
  the generated client.                                                       
                                                                              
  #### 1. Serve  GET /api/_describe                                           
                                                                              
  • Route: Added  DESCRIBE_PATH = '/_describe'  under the API base path (     
  /api/_describe ).                                                           
  • Gate: Gated as  public  so anonymous callers (e.g. schema-driven UI /     
  models during boot) can inspect exposed contracts and auth levels before    
  sign-in without triggering 401s (unblocking surfdns#40).                    
  • Deny-by-default for internal contracts:  descriptorFor  calls             
  describeExposure  with  allowInternal: false . Any internal contracts       
  exposed by a site fail closed and return 500  INTERNAL_CONTRACT .           
  • Headers & Caching: Emits  x-exposure-shape: descriptor.shapeHash  and     
  deliberately omits  x-exposure  (as clients check stale shape independently 
  of site-specific exposure). Carries  etag: descriptor.exposure  and  cache- 
  control: no-cache , returning 304 on matching  If-None-Match . Returns 409  
  EXPOSURE_MISMATCH  if client presents a differing  x-exposure-shape .       
                                                                              
